<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Ms. Joie talked about the historic shift in framing from the global north to the global south: recognition that it is about the global majority vs major polluters, with a small minority causing immense harm. This helped to decolonize the condition and narrative of climate change. North negotiated itself down at the ICJ; it demonstrated how powerful actors had to defend their responsibilities within an international legal framework. She also addressed the whole process of reframing climate change as climate justice, which moves beyond a purely scientific and technical discourse and highlights the moral, ethical, and justice dimensions at the core of the issue.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
