199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Facilitated by Ms. Swikriti Timsina and Mr. Hemant Kandel, the Ekota platform connected directly with those youth voices who are vulnerable and marginalized. The channel was created as Youth Conversation, South Asian Climate Justice, comprising 300 participants. There were altogether 13 groups that explored the theme of mental health in climate resilience, bridging glacial risks, from global benchmarks to national action, recent glacier outburst of Nepal, climate finance and economic resilience, climate justice and youth distress migration in South Asia, human development due to Climate induced, coastal eco system, blue carbon eco system, livelihood of marginalized farmers, policy recommendations for advancing climate justice in Nepal and Pakistan and Comparative analysis of food sovereignty in Nepal and Bhutan under Climate Change.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [16]
>>
