262 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Facilitated by Ms. Shreya KC, the session explained that climate finance is encouraged but not mandatory, often favoring mitigation and coming as loans rather than grants, which burdens developing nations. Historical emitters have greater responsibility, but emerging emitters also share duties. Current challenges include broken promises and misuse, with solutions like the polluter pays principle, solidarity levies, and aviation and shipping taxes.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [13]
>>
