/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The South Asian Climate Justice camp, 2025, played a pivotal role in directly connecting with youth voices and fostering cross-border solidarity in South Asia. Over the three days, the participants engaged in the discussion of climate justice and climate regime, International Court of Justice, Advisory Opinion \(ICJ-AO\), climate finance, loss and damage, sustainable practices, climate and policy advocacy, capacity building, and the Ekota platform. Despite minor challenges in time management and the session's adjustments, the camp still served its core objectives. Lastly, the camp has been successful with strong commitments toward policy advocacy, community engagement, and regional cooperation. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [15 16]
